BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rethinking Stress: How to Turn Negative Stress into a Powerful For
 ce!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T193000
UID:69c29dc423b45fff20f2ec89@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to develop greater awareness of your stress levels and e
 xplore healthy strategies for fostering calmness and groundedness . During
  this presentation\, we will define good and bad stress and anxiety\, body
  symptoms\, the cost of stress\, how to make stress your friend\, and body
 -oriented ways to work with stress.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Small Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c29dc423b45fff20f2ec89
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
