UID:69e2b76b129f12743839378c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Mindful Monday to make a worry doll with yarn. Or
 iginating from the Guatemalan Mayan tradition\, worry dolls were handmade 
 to help youth manage their fears and anxieties. While traditionally made f
 rom wire\, wood\, and colourful textiles\, we will make our own version wi
 th soft yarn. Whisper your anxieties to your doll\, place it under your pi
 llow at night\, and let your doll take your worries away by morning.\nThis
  is a drop-in Youth Hub program for teens.\nAll materials provided.\nThis 
 program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for
  teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always ava
